    <bpmn:process id="W_W1189" name="W1189. Cement &amp; Bagged Material Shelf Life Expiry Monitoring &amp; Proactive Markdown" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: System shelf life monitoring job (daily batch check)
Frequency: Daily monitoring; weekly proactive markdown execution
Volume: ~500–800 cement/bagged material lots across 200 stores + 4 DCs at any time; ~20–50 lots approaching expiry monthly
Owner: Category Manager (Building Materials)
Participants: Category Manager, Store Manager, Inventory Accountant, Pricing Analyst, Purchasing Manager
Source: workflow W1189 — Cement &amp; Bagged Material Shelf Life Expiry Monitoring &amp; Proactive Markdown</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1189_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1189_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1189_Lane2" name="Pricing Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1189_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1189_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1189_Start5" name="System shelf life monitoring job (daily batch check)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1189_Task6" name="Daily shelf life batch check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily shelf life batch check: System runs daily batch job scanning all cement/bagged material lots; calculates days remaining to expiry based on manufacturing date + shelf life months (configurable per SKU: cement 90 days, tile adhesive 180 days, grout 180 days, mortar mix 90 days); flags lots at three thresholds: (a) T-60 days (amber alert — approaching expiry), (b) T-30 days (red alert — markdown trigger), (c) T-0 days (expired — block from sale)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1189_Task7" name="Weekly expiry report distribution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Weekly expiry report distribution: Every Monday, system generates &quot;Bagged Material Shelf Life Report&quot; showing: (a) all lots at T-60 and T-30, (b) by store/DC, (c) by vendor/brand, (d) quantity and value at risk; distributes to Category Manager, affected Store Managers, and Purchasing Manager
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1189_Task8" name="Proactive markdown at T-30">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Proactive markdown at T-30: For lots at T-30 threshold: Pricing Analyst applies graduated markdown schedule: (a) T-30: 20% off SRP, (b) T-15: 40% off SRP, (c) T-7: 60% off SRP; system updates price and generates shelf labels; store staff re-tags items; POS applies markdown automatically; markdowns are promoted in-store as &quot;Closeout — Best Before [date]&quot; to maintain transparency
Responsible (R): Pricing Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1189_Task9" name="Inter-store/DC rebalancing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Inter-store/DC rebalancing: For lots at T-60 in low-demand stores with surplus: Category Manager initiates inter-store or store-to-DC transfer to high-demand stores where sell-through rate is faster; system prioritizes FIFO (First In, First Out) dispatch for all bagged materials
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Supply Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1189_Task10" name="Expired lot quarantine and block">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Expired lot quarantine and block: At T-0: system automatically changes inventory status to &quot;Expired — Blocked from Sale&quot;; POS rejects scan of expired lot; Store Manager physically quarantines expired items in designated area; items cannot be sold for structural use
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/lot</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1189_Task11" name="Expired material disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Expired material disposition: (a) Vendor return: if vendor accepts expired stock for recycling (cement can be ground and reprocessed), coordinate RTV per W88 with vendor credit; (b) Non-structural donation: expired cement can be donated to LGUs for non-structural use (road base, landfill cover); coordinate with CSR team per W1106; (c) Disposal: if no recovery option, dispose per non-hazardous waste protocol (W502); system writes off inventory per W92
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Inventory Accountant
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 30 min/lot</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1189_Task12" name="Root cause analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Root cause analysis: Monthly: Category Manager and Purchasing Manager review expiry write-off report: (a) write-off rate by vendor (target: &lt; 1% of bagged material purchases), (b) write-off rate by store (flag stores &gt; 2%), (c) purchasing lot size vs. sell-through rate; adjust purchase order quantities and safety stock levels for high-expiry SKUs; vendor quality issues (e.g., short shelf life on delivery) feed into vendor scorecard per W44
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Purchasing Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1189_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1189_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1189_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1189_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: automated POS block in Step 5 and graduated markdown in Step 3 to ensure stock sells before expiry; operational: using conservative shelf life settings (90 days vs. 120 days) and palletized covered storage; operational: smaller, more frequent orders and vendor-managed inventory (W20) for high-volume cement brands
Owner: Category Manager (Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1189_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1189_Annotation14" targetRef="W1189_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
