    <bpmn:process id="W_W1216" name="W1216. Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Replenishment Monitoring &amp; Exception Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: VMI vendor transmits replenishment proposal or ASN; or system detects VMI SKU inventory below safety stock without vendor replenishment; or daily VMI dashboard review
Frequency: Daily monitoring; weekly exception review with VMI vendors
Volume: ~300 SKUs from 12 VMI vendors across 200 stores and 4 DCs = ~60,000 SKU-location combinations
Owner: Supply Planning Analyst
Participants: Supply Planning Analyst, Vendor VMI Coordinator, DC Supervisor, Merchandise Planner, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1216 — Vendor-Managed Inventory (VMI) Replenishment Monitoring &amp; Exception Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1216_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1216_Lane1" name="Supply Planning Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1216_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1216_Lane3" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1216_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1216_Start5" name="VMI vendor transmits replenishment proposal or ASN; or system detects VMI SKU inventory…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task6" name="Daily VMI dashboard review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily VMI dashboard review: Supply Planning Analyst opens VMI monitoring dashboard showing: (a) all VMI SKU-locations with current stock level vs. min/max, (b) items below minimum (replenishment overdue), (c) items at zero stock (critical stockout), (d) pending vendor ASNs and expected delivery dates, (e) items above maximum (potential overstock — vendor over-shipping), (f) VMI fill rate trend (target: ≥ 98%)
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task7" name="Exception triage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Exception triage: for items below minimum or at zero stock: (a) check if vendor has transmitted ASN for replenishment — if yes, verify ETA is within acceptable window; (b) if no ASN received and stock below minimum for &gt; 2 days: system generates automated alert to vendor VMI Coordinator; (c) for zero-stock critical items: Supply Planning Analyst contacts vendor VMI Coordinator immediately for expedited replenishment
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 30 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task8" name="Overstock management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Overstock management: for items above maximum stock level: (a) Supply Planning Analyst notifies vendor to pause replenishment shipments; (b) if vendor has already shipped over-max quantity: DC Supervisor holds excess in receiving (not putaway) per agreement; (c) Category Manager evaluates if overstock is due to demand drop — may need min/max parameter adjustment
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst / DC Supervisor
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1216_Task9" name="Vendor ASN validation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Vendor ASN validation: when vendor transmits replenishment ASN: (a) system auto-compares ASN quantities against VMI min/max parameters — flags if quantity exceeds max or is below minimum, (b) system validates SKU, quantity, location, and expected ship date against VMI agreement terms, (c) if ASN is within parameters: system auto-approves and creates expected receipt in WMS per W109, (d) if ASN is out of parameters: routes to Supply Planning Analyst for manual review
Responsible (R): System / Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min/day manual review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task10" name="Weekly VMI vendor scorecard review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly VMI vendor scorecard review: Supply Planning Analyst compiles weekly scorecard per VMI vendor: (a) fill rate (orders fulfilled vs. demanded), (b) on-time delivery rate, (c) overstock frequency, (d) ASN accuracy, (e) average days below minimum; shares with Category Manager for vendor relationship management per W44
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1 hour/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task11" name="Quarterly VMI parameter review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly VMI parameter review: Category Manager and Supply Planning Analyst review VMI parameters with each vendor: (a) are min/max levels still appropriate based on current demand trends?, (b) should SKUs be added or removed from VMI program?, (c) is order frequency optimal?, (d) review and adjust safety stock calculations based on demand variability; update VMI agreement parameters in system
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Supply Planning Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/vendor/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1216_Task12" name="Annual VMI program evaluation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual VMI program evaluation: Category Manager evaluates overall VMI program: (a) compare VMI item in-stock rate vs. non-VMI items, (b) total VMI savings (reduced planning labor, improved turns) vs. VMI management cost, (c) identify candidates for VMI expansion (additional vendors/SKUs) or VMI removal (vendors not meeting SLA), (d) present recommendation to VP Merchandising
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1 day/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1216_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1216_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1216_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1216_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: Supply Planning Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Planning Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
