    <bpmn:process id="W_W1257" name="W1257. Seasonal Inventory Pre-Positioning, Forward-Buy Execution &amp; Phase-Out Calendar Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Scheduled — triggered by seasonal merchandise calendar milestones (6 major seasonal transitions per year); ad-hoc triggered by PAGASA weather advisory, commodity price surge, or competitor stock-out opportunity
Frequency: 6 major seasonal cycles per year + ad-hoc pre-positioning events; forward-buy execution per import PO cycle
Volume: ~500 seasonal/promotional SKUs per cycle; forward-buy quantities of 3–6 months&#x27; supply for select A-class seasonal items; phase-out of ~100–200 SKUs per seasonal transition
Owner: Merchandise Planner / Category Manager
Participants: Buyer, Demand Planner, Import Coordinator, DC Operations Manager, Store Manager, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1257 — Seasonal Inventory Pre-Positioning, Forward-Buy Execution &amp; Phase-Out Calendar Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1257_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1257_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1257_Lane2" name="Import Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1257_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1257_Start4" name="Scheduled — triggered by seasonal merchandise calendar milestones (6 major seasonal…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1257_Task5" name="Seasonal demand planning &amp; forward-buy decision">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal demand planning &amp; forward-buy decision: 90 days before season start, Category Manager and Demand Planner review: (a) prior year seasonal sales by SKU and store cluster; (b) current inventory on-hand of seasonal SKUs; (c) import PO lead time requirements (45–90 days); (d) commodity price trends and FX rates for import items; (e) decide forward-buy quantity: (i) standard buy: cover 60% of forecasted demand (remaining 40% from local vendors with shorter lead times), (ii) aggressive forward-buy: cover 100% of forecast if import pricing is favorable and storage capacity exists; (f) create seasonal buy plan with SKU-level quantities and delivery schedule
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 8 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1257_Task6" name="DC pre-positioning execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: DC pre-positioning execution: Import Coordinator and DC Operations Manager coordinate pre-season inventory positioning: (a) reserve DC storage space for incoming seasonal inventory — negotiate with standard stock allocation; (b) receive seasonal imports at DC per import PO schedule; (c) QC seasonal items (especially Christmas lights, flood control pumps, seasonal paint colors) for quality and compliance; (d) stage pre-positioned inventory in designated seasonal zone at each DC; (e) generate store allocation plan based on: (i) regional demand patterns (rainy season items higher in flood-prone areas, garden higher in Metro Manila), (ii) store size tier, (iii) prior year sell-through performance
Responsible (R): Import Coordinator / DC Operations Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 16 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1257_Task7" name="Seasonal transition execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Seasonal transition execution: 2 weeks before season start, execute store-level transition: (a) push first allocation of seasonal stock to stores via replenishment order; (b) store receives seasonal goods and sets up seasonal display per planogram; (c) markdown previous season&#x27;s remaining inventory per W93 — target: 50% markdown for items within 2 weeks of season end; (d) transfer remaining previous-season inventory to clearance stores or central clearance zone per W220; (e) system updates seasonal flag on items — active season items get priority replenishment, expiring season items enter markdown countdown
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 4 hours/store allocation + 2 hours/store transition</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1257_Task8" name="In-season monitoring &amp; replenishment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: In-season monitoring &amp; replenishment: During active season: (a) weekly sell-through review for seasonal SKUs — compare actual to forecast; (b) for overperforming SKUs (sell-through &gt; 120% of forecast): trigger emergency replenishment from local vendors or reallocate from lower-performing stores; (c) for underperforming SKUs (sell-through &lt; 60% of forecast): reduce replenishment, increase markdown depth, or initiate return-to-vendor; (d) monitor competitor seasonal activity — adjust pricing or promotion if competitor undercuts; (e) 4 weeks before season end: begin aggressive markdown for remaining seasonal stock
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Demand Planner
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/week during season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1257_Task9" name="Post-season phase-out &amp; lessons learned">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-season phase-out &amp; lessons learned: Within 2 weeks of season end: (a) final disposition of remaining seasonal inventory: markdown to clearance, return-to-vendor (if agreement permits), or donate (CSR tax benefit per W193); (b) conduct post-season review: (i) forecast accuracy by SKU, (ii) forward-buy ROI — did bulk import purchase save cost vs. spot buying? (iii) markdown cost vs. inventory carrying cost — was forward-buy quantity optimal? (iv) store-level performance variation; (c) document lessons learned for next season&#x27;s buy plan; (d) update seasonal planning parameters in system per W312
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 8 hours/season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1257_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1257_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1257_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1257_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: Merchandise Planner / Category Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Merchandise Planner / Category Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
