        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1258_Lane4" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1258_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1258_Lane5" name="Inventory Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1258_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1258_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1258_Start7" name="Scheduled — monthly aging analysis refresh; weekly dashboard update; ad-hoc triggered by…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1258_Task8" name="Weekly aging dashboard refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly aging dashboard refresh: System automatically calculates inventory aging for all SKU-locations: (a) age bucket distribution: 0–30 days (current), 31–90 days (aging), 91–180 days (slow-moving), 181–365 days (obsolescence risk), &gt; 365 days (write-down candidate); (b) aging value by bucket: total WAC value in each aging bucket by location, category, and vendor; (c) trend vs. prior week: is aging inventory increasing or decreasing?; (d) flag SKU-locations where aging crossed a threshold in the past week (e.g., moved from 31–90 to 91–180 days)
Responsible (R): System / Inventory Controller
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1 hour/week (review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1258_Task9" name="Monthly NRV analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly NRV analysis: At month-end, Finance Analyst runs NRV analysis for aging inventory: (a) for SKU-locations in 91–180 day bucket: calculate NRV = current SRP × (1 – expected selling cost %) – expected disposal cost; (b) for SKU-locations in &gt; 180 day bucket: calculate NRV using clearance/markdown price (expected realizable value); (c) compare NRV to WAC — flag items where NRV &lt; WAC (write-down required); (d) calculate total write-down exposure by category and location; (e) generate write-down recommendation report for Finance Controller review
Responsible (R): Finance Analyst
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 8 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1258_Task10" name="Write-down approval &amp; posting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Write-down approval &amp; posting: Finance Controller reviews write-down recommendations: (a) validate NRV assumptions — are the clearance prices realistic? are the selling cost estimates accurate?; (b) approve or adjust write-down amounts; (c) for write-downs &gt; PHP 500,000 per category: escalate to CFO for approval; (d) post approved write-downs to GL — debit inventory write-down expense, credit inventory reserve; (e) update item cost records to reflect new carrying value
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1258_Task11" name="Aging exception management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Aging exception management: Category Manager reviews aging exceptions and takes action: (a) for items in 91–180 day bucket: evaluate markdown, promotional bundle, or store-to-store transfer to higher-demand location; (b) for items in &gt; 180 day bucket: initiate clearance sale, return-to-vendor negotiation, or donation for tax benefit; (c) for items in &gt; 365 day bucket: approve for disposal per W91/W587; (d) system tracks action taken per aging exception — target: all exceptions addressed within 30 days
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1258_Task12" name="Quarterly aging trend analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quarterly aging trend analysis: Inventory Controller produces quarterly trend report: (a) aging distribution trend — is the proportion of aging inventory increasing?; (b) write-down trend — is write-down expense increasing by category?; (c) top 20 aging SKUs by value — what&#x27;s driving the aging? (slow category, wrong assortment, import over-buy?); (d) location-level aging heat map — which stores and DCs have the highest aging concentration?; (e) present findings to CFO and VP Merchandising with recommendations
Responsible (R): Inventory Controller
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 8 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1258_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1258_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1258_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1258_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: Inventory Controller / Finance Analyst review and approval gate
Owner: Inventory Controller / Finance Analyst</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1258_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1258_Annotation14" targetRef="W1258_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
