      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1298" name="W1298. Consignment Inventory Reconciliation, Settlement &amp; Ownership Transfer Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Monthly consignment reconciliation cycle; or vendor request for sales report; or inventory count discrepancy
Frequency: Monthly reconciliation per vendor; weekly sales data transmission to consignment vendors
Volume: ~300 consignment SKUs across 200 stores; ~15–25 consignment vendors (per the register); ~PHP 150–200M in consignment inventory at any time
Owner: Category Manager (Merchandising)
Participants: Category Manager, AP Clerk, Store Department Supervisor, Vendor Consignment Coordinator, Finance Controller
Source: workflow W1298 — Consignment Inventory Reconciliation, Settlement &amp; Ownership Transfer Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1298_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1298_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1298_Lane2" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1298_Lane3" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1298_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1298_Start5" name="Monthly consignment reconciliation cycle; or vendor request for sales report; or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1298_Task6" name="Weekly consignment sales data transmission">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly consignment sales data transmission: System automatically compiles weekly consignment sales report per vendor: (a) items sold (SKU, quantity, store, date, POS transaction number), (b) consignment cost per unit and total cost payable, (c) retail price and BuildRight margin, (d) current consignment inventory on-hand by store; report transmitted to vendor via supplier portal per W224
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1298_Task7" name="Monthly consignment inventory reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Monthly consignment inventory reconciliation: Monthly, Category Manager and Vendor Consignment Coordinator reconcile: (a) system-generated consignment inventory report vs. vendor&#x27;s own inventory records, (b) identify discrepancies: (i) system shows sold but vendor disagrees (possible POS scanning error — item scanned against wrong SKU), (ii) vendor shows sold but system does not (possible unreported sale or inventory shrinkage), (iii) quantity mismatch at specific stores; (c) for discrepancies: Store Department Supervisor conducts physical count of affected consignment SKUs; (d) reconciliation target: discrepancies resolved within 5 business days; (e) system-adjusted consignment inventory quantities posted with Category Manager approval
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Vendor Consignment Coordinator
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 4–8 hours/vendor/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1298_Task8" name="Monthly settlement &amp; AP processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Monthly settlement &amp; AP processing: (a) upon reconciliation agreement, system generates consignment settlement invoice: total units sold × consignment cost per unit = amount payable to vendor; (b) AP Clerk reviews settlement invoice against reconciliation report and POS sales records; (c) system creates AP voucher per vendor with payment terms per consignment agreement (typically Net 30 from settlement date); (d) Finance Controller approves payment batch; (e) payment released per standard AP calendar per W7
Responsible (R): System / AP Clerk
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/vendor/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1298_Task9" name="Damaged / defective consignment inventory processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Damaged / defective consignment inventory processing: (a) Store Department Supervisor identifies damaged consignment item (display damage, customer damage, DOA for appliances); (b) creates damage report with photos in ERP; (c) system routes damage report to vendor via supplier portal with request for disposition: (i) vendor picks up and replaces — most common for major appliances, (ii) vendor authorizes destroy-in-place with full credit — for fragile items where return shipping exceeds value, (iii) vendor authorizes markdown-at-cost — BuildRight sells at reduced price, vendor accepts reduced settlement; (d) damaged items segregated in backroom pending vendor response (not mixed with owned damaged goods)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 15–30 min per incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1298_Task10" name="Consignment-to-owned inventory transfer">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Consignment-to-owned inventory transfer: When vendor agrees to convert consignment stock to owned inventory (e.g., vendor discontinues consignment arrangement or offers a discounted buyout): (a) Category Manager negotiates transfer terms — typically at a discount to regular consignment cost (10–25% below consignment rate) to incentivize BuildRight to take ownership; (b) system processes inventory ownership transfer: (i) remove items from consignment inventory bucket, (ii) add to owned inventory at transfer cost (becomes new WAC), (iii) create AP voucher for transferred items payable per agreed terms; (c) Finance Controller approves transfer and payment; (d) transferred items become regular inventory managed per standard replenishment and markdown processes
Responsible (R): Category Manager / Finance Controller
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–4 hours per transfer event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1298_Task11" name="Quarterly consignment program performance review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Quarterly consignment program performance review: Category Manager reviews consignment program ROI: (a) consignment inventory turn rate vs. owned inventory turn rate, (b) margin comparison: consignment margin vs. owned margin for similar categories, (c) shrinkage and damage cost allocation (vendor vs. BuildRight), (d) working capital benefit: consignment inventory value not on BuildRight&#x27;s balance sheet, (e) recommend to VP Merchandising: expand consignment to additional vendors/SKUs, convert underperforming consignment to owned, or terminate consignment with vendors not meeting SLA
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2 hours/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1298_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1298_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1298_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1298_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: Category Manager (Merchandising) review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Category Manager (Merchandising)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1298_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1298_Annotation13" targetRef="W1298_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
