    <bpmn:process id="W_W1437" name="W1437. Store-Level Building Material Damaged Package Reconditioning &amp; Resaleable Recovery Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Store Associate identifies merchandise with damaged packaging but intact product during shelf replenishment or customer return; or weekly damaged goods review cycle
Frequency: ~4–8 items per store per month with reconditionable damage; ~800–1,600 items/month chain-wide (~200–370/week; a ~25–35% subset of W91&#x27;s total damage volume)
Volume: ~60–80% of items with packaging damage can be reconditioned and resold at full or reduced price; ~PHP 2,000–5,000 average item value for building materials
Owner: Department Supervisor
Participants: Department Supervisor, Stock Associate, Store Manager, Category Manager (for markdown decisions)
Source: workflow W1437 — Store-Level Building Material Damaged Package Reconditioning &amp; Resaleable Recovery Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1437_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1437_Lane1" name="Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1437_Lane2" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1437_Lane3" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1437_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1437_Start5" name="Store Associate identifies merchandise with damaged packaging but intact product during…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1437_Task6" name="Damage identification and classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Damage identification and classification: Stock Associate or Department Supervisor identifies item with damaged packaging during shelf replenishment or customer return; classify damage severity: (a) Level 1 (minor): label damage, minor box creasing, blister pack torn but product intact — reconditionable for full price, (b) Level 2 (moderate): significant box damage, dented can, torn bag but product intact — reconditionable at markdown, (c) Level 3 (severe): product damaged or contaminated — route to W91 (damaged goods disposition)
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 3 min per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1437_Task7" name="Level 1 reconditioning (full-price resale)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Level 1 reconditioning (full-price resale): For Level 1 items: (a) Stock Associate replaces damaged label with system-printed replacement label (barcode, SRP, item description), (b) re-boxes or re-bags item using generic packaging supplies stocked at each store (brown wrapping paper, plain boxes, cable ties, packing tape), (c) verifies product integrity (weigh/measure if catch-weight), (d) returns to shelf with standard SRP — no markdown required
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1437_Task8" name="Level 2 reconditioning (markdown resale)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Level 2 reconditioning (markdown resale): For Level 2 items: (a) Department Supervisor determines markdown percentage: 10–20% for cosmetic packaging damage, 20–30% for significant packaging damage with exposed product, (b) Store Manager authorizes markdown if &gt; 20%, (c) system generates markdown label with original SRP and markdown price clearly displayed, (d) item placed on dedicated &quot;Open Box / Damaged Packaging&quot; rack near checkout or in applicable department, (e) POS scans original barcode; system applies markdown price from markdown authorization
Responsible (R): Department Supervisor / Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min per item</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1437_Task9" name="Reconditioning supplies management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Reconditioning supplies management: Store maintains reconditioning supply kit: (a) replacement labels (thermal printer stock), (b) generic boxes (5 sizes), (c) brown wrapping paper and bubble wrap, (d) cable ties and strapping, (e) packing tape, (f) &quot;Open Box&quot; shelf tags; Stock Associate monitors supply levels and requests replenishment from DC via standard replenishment order when supplies run low
Responsible (R): Stock Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1437_Task10" name="Weekly reconditioning report">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Weekly reconditioning report: Store Manager compiles weekly reconditioning summary: (a) items reconditioned by level (L1, L2), (b) recovery value: L1 items at full price, L2 items at markdown — total revenue recovered, (c) items routed to disposition (L3) — unrecoverable loss, (d) report submitted to Regional Manager for trend analysis; stores with high L3 rates flagged for root cause investigation (receiving damage, vendor packaging quality)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Regional Manager
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1437_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1437_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1437_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1437_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-255 (ensure controlled execution — Inventory Disposition &amp; Optimization (PA-05.3).) | - operational: manager authorization requirement for markdowns &gt; 20% and audit trail per W1174
Owner: Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
